okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Follow up the Walkie support request (Claude Doc 3534f7f4, 'Ciel Runtime 기술지원 요청 — 채널 메시지가 superseded 로 버려짐'): distinct Walkie messages skipped as superseded, one message per busy period, wrong input status."
reported: "User, 2026-09-23: '이 요청사항 팔로어웁. g:\ciel-walkie 에서 나온' with the doc link."
cause_confirmed:
  superseded_key: "channel_message_policy.message_coalesce_key built (source, channel, method, kind, topic) = ('ciel-runtime-external-event', 'external:default', '', 'com.ciel.walkie.support.message', '') for every Walkie event: thread_id, event_id and event_source are not part of it, and event_id is not in _UNIQUE_REFERENCE_META_KEYS. Order falls back to (3, local queue id) because the Walkie event_id is not numeric. So every later Walkie event superseded every earlier one still unread. Replay of the real queue (instance aae7db361c7f runtime-inputs.jsonl, 732 rows, all external events): 730 ids superseded before the fix, 0 after."
  which_path_dropped: "Router log lines are channel_llm_inject_skipped (router-side channel_llm_context). That path commits the shared cursor past a superseded id (max_seen), so the launcher never scanned those ids again; runtime-input-status kept them at queued because no skip status existed."
  count_1: "channel_pending_injection: batch_limit was 1 unless wake_for_llm_delivery, and a non-router candidate always broke after one message ('TUI/session-socket draft carries exactly one request')."
  stale_unconfirmed_a: "Session-socket (peer) user records are isMeta:true + origin.kind=peer; is_non_turn_user_record treated them as bookkeeping, so they were never delivery evidence (669 etc.)."
  stale_unconfirmed_b: "Message 714: Claude Code wrote queue-operation enqueue, then remove, then attachment queued_command, and the next assistant record acted on it (Bash 'Record tag push event 6869'). wake_state_evidence counted the attachment only as 'queued', and queued_dropped_from_text treated the remove as a drop (dropped stayed True even after the attachment) -> released stale_unconfirmed. In the real Walkie transcript all 216 queued_command attachments directly follow a remove, and 215 are followed by an assistant record (1 by a user record)."
changes:
  - "channel_message_policy.message_coalesce_key: external events that carry an event_id are never coalesced. Progress-style notices without event_id still coalesce."
  - "channel_transcript.is_non_turn_user_record: origin.kind == peer is a real turn (affects typed-prompt evidence and turn-active projection)."
  - "channel_transcript.wake_state_evidence_from_text: a queued_command attachment seen after a matching queue remove counts as the delivered prompt (same not_before horizon). queued_dropped_from_text: that attachment clears dropped."
  - "runtime_input_status: new terminal state skipped (queued -> skipped; untracked ids write nothing). ChannelWakeDeliveryRepository.skip; launcher path records superseded_channel_notice / duplicate_channel_event, router path (ChannelLlmContextRepository.mark_skipped) and the codex-desktop injector record superseded_channel_notice."
  - "channel_pending_injection: session_socket candidates batch up to CIEL_RUNTIME_CHANNEL_WAKE_BATCH_LIMIT (default 8) with the same batch key; TTY stays one per draft."
  - "tests/test_channel_walkie_delivery.py (8 tests, fixtures copied from the real 707 row and the 714 record order)."
verification:
  real_data_replay: "superseded_message_ids over the real 732-row queue: 730 -> 0. wake_state_from_text over the real Walkie transcript for the 8 ids >= 640 recorded failed/stale_unconfirmed (660, 669, 677, 690, 695, 714, 722, 731): all 'completed' after (before the change 669 and 714 evaluated 'queued'; the other six were not evaluated before)."
  tests: "Final: unit 1608 OK (skipped=45), router 1153 OK, runtime 320 OK (skipped=19), channel 434 OK (skipped=80); ruff clean on ciel_runtime_support, tests, ciel_runtime.py; ciel_runtime.py 4980 lines (unchanged)."
  flaky_note: "In two channel-group runs started right after the long unit/router runs, test_channel_transcript_repository BoundaryScanDeadlineTests (two tests with 0.1 s scan deadlines) failed. Not reproduced in 6 group runs with the changes and 6 without, nor in 12 file-only runs. Cause not confirmed."
  not_done: "Not committed, pushed or deployed; the Walkie session still runs 0.2.51. The live E2E is under turn_gate_root_fix.e2e."
request_item_4_receipt: "external_event_receiver._run_sse writes the SSE cursor (sent back as Last-Event-ID) right after _admit appends the event to runtime-inputs.jsonl, i.e. after durable enqueue and before injection. How the Walkie server turns that into notification_receipts.accepted_sequence is Walkie-side and not checked. Not changed."
turn_gate_root_fix:
  cause: "channel_pending_poll.poll_pending_channel_messages returned before inject_pending whenever services.active() (Windows: active tool call or console turn; POSIX: input_busy). The gate dates from 2026-07-18 (7c0864f, cf41ddb) when TTY typing was the only transport; session_socket came on 2026-09-01/03 (60846f9, cd32b97) with its mid-turn exemption only inside inject_pending, which the gate made unreachable. Claude's default transport is session_socket (ciel_runtime.py _default_channel_input_transport)."
  measurement: "Isolated Claude Code 2.1.278 + fake upstream holding the main turn stream 20 s: a socket frame sent at +3 s was enqueued immediately (queue enqueue 18:07:58), dequeued at the turn end (18:08:15) and delivered as the next user record (isMeta, origin peer); the next model request carried it."
  change: "ChannelPendingPollServices.session_socket_ready (wired from _CLAUDE_SESSION_SOCKET.available through ChannelTerminalPollingPorts/ChannelTerminalPolling). While busy, the scan still runs when the socket is ready and new input arrived or the safety rescan is due; inject_pending keeps deferring TTY inputs; pending_recheck stays set so TTY inputs are retried at the turn end."
  confirmation_backlog: "Mid-turn socket injections arrive one per scan, and the poll tracked only the newest inflight id: first E2E run left 4 and 5 at submitted while 6 was replied. ChannelPendingInflightState.backlog keeps the earlier ids; they are promoted when the current one completes or fails."
  e2e: "ciel_runtime.py cli --ca-runtime claude (Claude Code 2.1.280, provider deepseek via isolated e2e-cfg, router 19945, ConPTY). Prompt ran a 45 s PowerShell sleep through Bash; 8 s into it three Walkie-shaped external events (room-a x2, room-b, distinct event_ids, input_transport session_socket) were POSTed to /ca/chat/notify. Router: claude_session_socket_injected + channel_stdin_proxy_injected for 7, 8, 9 at 13:34:55-57. Transcript: queue enqueue 18:34:55/56/57Z, tool_result SLEEP_DONE 18:35:39Z, queue remove x3 18:35:40Z, queued_command attachments, three mcp send_message replies, end_turn 'FINISHED'. Router: channel_windows_console_confirmed 9, 7, 8; status 7, 8, 9 = replied."
  e2e_hazards: "Run 3 reused event_ids and was correctly dropped as chat_message_skipped_duplicate. Runs 1-3 inherited this session's CLAUDE_* variables (CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, ...) and the child Claude wrote no transcript anywhere under the user profile; with CLAUDE*/ANTHROPIC_* stripped (runs 4-5) it wrote one normally. Whether those variables are the reason is not confirmed."
  still_not_done: "Not committed, pushed or deployed. Walkie itself was not driven."
